From 8f541fdc33fb8cf67b11508213912890f9f0b595 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:48:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(project)!: step the file to v78 for stored tool
 reservations

PR #3485 merged first and took project version 77 for the setup
`order` key (#3447). The stored machine `reserved_tools` field now
takes version 78. Main's v77 meaning is unchanged.

The step is a pure step-up: a v77 file opens with no change. The pins
`saved_machine_reservations_need_the_v78_reader` and
`a_v77_machine_steps_up_with_no_reservation` hold the step.

BREAKING CHANGE: the project file version is 78. A build that reads
version 77 or lower refuses each project that this build saves. The
refusal is deliberate: an older reader would drop the machine's
`reserved_tools` and could post a cutting tool at a reserved probe
pocket. Projects of older builds open with no change.

Fixes #2604

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
